      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Replace `#define` Macros with `constexpr` Variables (`iapcontrol.cc`)**\nIn C, macros are standard for constants. However, in C++, macros are heavily discouraged because they bypass scope, lack type safety, and make debugging harder. \n*   **Action:** Replace your macros with `constexpr` variables inside an **anonymous namespace**. This ensures strict type safety (no casting needed when assigning to your `uint8_t` buffers) and ensures the constants don\u0027t leak into other files.\n    ```cpp\n    namespace ElanApp {\n    namespace {\n        // Safe, typed, and scoped to this file only\n        constexpr uint8_t kCmdRunIap \u003d 0x20;\n        constexpr uint8_t kErrStaSuccess \u003d 0x01;\n        constexpr size_t kEp1Length \u003d 8;\n        // ... (update the rest similarly)\n    } \n    }\n    ```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "656b174d3c9ed84c1437f3e1b4fd98c8b82106ea",
