      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Bug / Memory Safety: Unmatched `libusb_exit`**\nIn the destructor, `libusb_exit(nullptr)` is called unconditionally. If an `IapControl` object is created but `initialize()` is never called, `libusb_exit(nullptr)` will be called without a matching `libusb_init(nullptr)`. This can lead to undefined behavior or a crash in the libusb library.\n*Remediation:* Keep track of whether `libusb_init` was successfully called (e.g., using a boolean flag `m_libusbInitialized`), and only call `libusb_exit` if it was.",
      "revId": "656b174d3c9ed84c1437f3e1b4fd98c8b82106ea",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
